the sense of परि-ग्लान, exhausted, (but पर्य्-
अध्ययन is said to mean ‘one to whom study is
repugnant.’) Native lexicographers explain the senses
of परि by the following Sanskrit words: आ-लिङ्गन,
दोषाख्यान (दोष-कीर्तन), निर्-असन (नि-
वसन), पूजा, भूषण, व्याधि, व्य्-आप्ति, उप-
रम, शोक, शेष, अति-शय, त्याग, नि-यम;
[cf. Zend pairi; Gr. περί, πέριξ, περι-σσό-ς, -περ;
Lat. per- in adj., e. g. per-idoneus: probably Old
Germ. furi; Old Iceland. fyri; Mod. Germ. für;
Hib. faoi, ‘about, round.’]

परि-गम, अस्, m. or परि-गमन, अम्, n.
going round, surrounding; spreading, extending;
knowing, ascertaining; obtaining.

परि-ग्राह, अस्, m. the fencing round (of the
Vedi or sacrificial altar with three lines or furrows;
if of the northern altar, called उत्तर-परिग्राह;
if of the eastern, पूर्व-परिग्राह).

परि-घातिन्, ई, इनी, इ, destroying, annihilating;
setting at nought; transgressing (e. g. in नृपाज्ञा-
परिघातिन्, transgressing the commands of a king).

परि-चरण, अस्, m. an assistant, a servant;
(अम्), n. going about; serving, attending upon,
attention to.

परिचि 1. परि-चि, cl. 5. P. A. -चिनोति, -नुते,
-चेतुम्, to pile up, heap up, accumulate; to collect;
to augment, increase; to gather in, acquire, obtain;
to fill with: Pass. -चीयते, to be increased or aug-
mented, to grow.

2. परि-च्छद्, त्, f. retinue, train, attendants;
paraphernalia; (at the end of a comp.) surrounded
by, provided with (see सेना-प्˚).

परि-च्युत, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen from, swerved
from; deprived of, lost; ruined; streaming with,
surrounded by streams (as of blood).

परि-ताप, अस्, m. glow, heat, scorching heat;
pain, anguish, grief, sorrow, affliction; fear, trembling;
N. of a particular hell.

परि-तापिन्, ई, इनी, इ, burning hot, very hot;
causing much pain or sorrow, causing anguish, tor-
turing, tormenting.

परि-देवित, अस्, आ, अम्, lamented, bewailed;
plaintive, lamenting, miserable; (अम्), n. lamentation,
wailing, complaint.

परि-धाय, अस्, m. train, retinue, attendants;
the hinder parts, posteriors; a receptacle for water,
reservoir.

परिध्वंस् परि-ध्वंस्, cl. 1. A. -ध्वंसते,
-ध्वंसितुम्, to fall to pieces, fall away, decay;
to be destroyed.

परि-ध्वंस, अस्, m. distress, disaster, ruin,
trouble, toil; failing, failure; injury, destruction;
leaving one's caste, loss of caste, mixture of castes.

परि-पाक, अस्, m. being completely cooked or
dressed; digestion; ripening, maturity, perfection;
the fruit or consequence of an action, consequence;
cleverness, shrewdness, experience.

परिपद् परि-पद्, त्, f., Ved. a snare, trap;
walking about; a creature, living being; (Sāy.) a
bird (as flying about).

परिपू परि-पू, cl. 9. P. A. -पुनाति, -नीते,
-पवितुम्, to purify completely, strain; to lustrate;
to become completely purified.

परि-प्रेप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ (fr. the Desid.), wishing
to reach, desirous of obtaining; wishing to defend;
desiring, desirous, seeking.

परि-भूय, ind. having treated with contempt,
having disgraced or despised; shaming, outvying;
experiencing disgrace.

परि-भ्रष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen off, dropped off;
fallen, cast down, degraded; escaped; vanished;
deprived of, void or devoid of (with abl. or some-
times inst.); lost; neglecting, omitting.
—परि-
भ्रष्ट-सुख, अस्, आ, अम्, fallen from happiness.

परि-भ्रम, अस्, आ, अम्, flying round or about
[cf. खे-प्˚]; (अस्), m. wandering, going about;
error; circumlocution, rambling discourse.

परि-मेय, अस्, आ, अम्, measurable, to be measured;
calculable, capable of being counted, few; finite.
—परिमेय-ता, f. measurableness, calculableness.

परिमृश् परि-मृश्, cl. 6. P. -मृशति, -मर्ष्-
टुम्, -म्रष्टुम्, to touch, handle, stroke, caress;
to grasp, seize; to examine, consider, reflect, ponder;
to investigate, inquire into, question; to observe,
discover: Intens. -मर्मर्ष्टि, Ved. to encompass,
clasp, embrace.

परि-मृश्य, ind. having touched or handled;
having grasped; having examined or pondered;
having found or observed.

परिवाप परि-वाप, अस्, m. (fr. rt. वप् with
परि), fried grains of rice; coagulated or thick sour
milk (= दधि, Ved.); furniture; a train, retinue;
sowing; a reservoir, pool, pond, piece of water;
shaving, shearing.

परि-वेषण, अम्, n. attendance, waiting, serving
up meals, distributing food; surrounding, enclosing;
circumference; a halo round the sun or moon.

परि-वर्तक, अस्, आ, अम्, turning round, turning
back; causing to turn round or flow back; causing
to revolve; bringing to a close; requiting, exchanging;
leaving off a thing begun for some other object;
(अस्), m., N. of a son of Duḥ-saha.

परि-वर्तन, अस्, ई, अम्, causing to turn round;
(ई), f. epithet of a particular magical art; (अम्), n.
cutting, clipping (the hair, Ved.); (according to a
Scholiast) = प्रेरण (Ved.); turning round, going
round, turning back, returning; moving to and fro;
whirling round, revolving; revolution, end of a
period of time; inverting, taking or putting anything
in a wrong direction; change, exchange, barter;
requital, return.

परि-वर्तित, अस्, आ, अम्, turned round, revolved;
returned, retreated; taken or put on in a wrong
direction; exchanged.

परिश्रय परि-श्रय, अस्, m. (fr. rt. श्रि with
परि), an enclosure, fence (Ved.); a refuge, asylum;
an assembly, meeting.

परि-ष्कन्दत् or परि-स्कन्दत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्,
leaping about, jumping round, going round or about;
surrounding, circumambulating; wandering.

परिस्था परि-स्था, cl. 1. P. A. -तिष्ठति,
-ते, -स्थातुम्, Ved. to stand round, encompass;
to obstruct (Sāy. = परि-वृत्य स्था).

परि-स्फुरत्, अन्, अती or अन्ती, अत्, quivering; dart-
ing, glancing, gleaming, moving quickly or suddenly;
budding, expanding; bursting forth.

परि-स्रव, अस्, m. (erroneously written परि-
श्रव), flowing, streaming, stream; a river, torrent;
birth (of a child); gliding down.

परि-हीण, अस्, आ, अम्, waned, faded, wasted;
deserted by; deprived of, destitute of; wanting,
deficient in (with abl.).

परि-हारक, अस्, इका, अम्, repelling, refuting;
(अस् or अम्), m. or n. ? (a various reading has
परि-हरक), an armlet; [cf. परि-हाटक.]

पारिभद्रक, अस्, m. the tree Erythrina Fulgens;
the Nimb tree, Azadirachta Indica; (अम्), n. Costus
Speciosus or Arabicus.
